**How to implement.** One place names each built-in identity (.spec-md §3.3; 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). This step moves the identity literals into two well-known id modules and deletes the Ui's `SeedEntryIds`. The preset ids keep their current text until step 20 mints their GUIDs, so every value and every fact is unchanged here. `SeedEntryIds` goes in the same step that adds `PresetIds`, because their shared names (`source600`, `detectorIntensity`, `polarizerLp`, `polarizerCpLeft`, `polarizerCpRight`) may not coexist (ELEV015). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, module `Library`, directly after `newSampleId` (`:47`): add `module SampleIds` and `module PresetIds`, plain modules shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:50-62`): no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`, no `[<Literal>]`, every member a typed value. They sit here and not in `MaterialLibrary.fs` because `SampleId` is declared at `:36` and this file compiles after `MaterialLibrary.fs`; `MaterialIds` and `CategoryIds` stay where they are. (a) `SampleIds` holds eleven `SampleId` values whose literals MOVE out of `SeedSamples` (each `id = Guid.Parse "…" |> SampleId` at `:655`, `:665`, `:675`, `:685`, `:695`, `:705`, `:732`, `:758`, `:768`, `:778`, `:788`): `glassPlate1mmId`, `glassPlate2mmId`, `glassFilm600Id`, `glassVacuumId`, `glassFilm200Id`, `multilayerQwId`, `euvMoSiId`, `uniaxialId`, `biaxialId`, `activeCrystalPlateId` and `langasiteSiliconId`. The `Id` suffix keeps each public name unique beside the same-named `SeedSamples` value (ELEV015), which S1.7 deletes. Each `SeedSamples` record reads its member (`id = SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`). (b) `PresetIds` holds 33 `ElementValueId` values, one per seeded preset, each written `ElementValueId "<its current id>"`: `source600` src-600; the `lasers` (`:832-846`) `heNe633` src-hene-633, `heNe543` src-hene-543, `argon488` src-ar-488, `argon515` src-ar-515, `heCd442` src-hecd-442, `heCd325` src-hecd-325, `diode405` src-diode-405, `ruby694` src-ruby-694, `tiSapphire800` src-tisa-800, `ndYag1064` src-ndyag-1064, `ndYag532` src-ndyag-532, `ndYag355` src-ndyag-355, `ndYag266` src-ndyag-266, `erbium1550` src-er-1550, `co2Laser10600` src-co2-10600; the `lithography` sources (`:853-860`) `mercuryG436` src-hg-g-436, `mercuryH405` src-hg-h-405, `mercuryI365` src-hg-i-365, `krf248` src-krf-248, `arf193` src-arf-193, `f2Excimer157` src-f2-157, `euv13p5` src-euv-13p5, `beuv6p7` src-beuv-6p7; the `tunables` (`:867-870`) `xenonMonochromator` src-xe-mono, `tiSapphireTunable` src-tisa-tunable, `supercontinuum` src-supercontinuum, `euvBeamline` src-euv-beamline; and (`:887-891`) `detectorIntensity` det-intensity, `detectorEllipsometer` det-ellipsometer, `polarizerLp` pol-lp, `polarizerCpLeft` pol-cp-left and `polarizerCpRight` pol-cp-right. `SeedSources` passes the members to `source` and `tunable` (`:827-870`); `seedEntries`' five detector and polarizer records (`:887-891`) and `seedTrees`' five detector and polarizer leaves (`:954-962`) read them, so each id is written once. (c) Docs, one to three lines each: `PresetIds` is the frozen identity of every seeded light-source, detector and polarizer preset, the one place a built-in preset's entry id is written (spec 0050 §3.3); `SampleIds` is the frozen identity of every seeded sample. `SampleId`'s doc (`:31-35`) and the `SeedSamples` doc (`:646-650`) say the fixed literals live in `SampleIds`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`, `detectorKindOf`'s doc (`:23-27`): the intensity and ellipsometer presets are named `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` / `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, not by their id text. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `module SeedEntryIds` and its doc (`:985-1000`) are deleted. `CatalogueKind.defaultSeedEntry` (`:1009-1014`) returns `Some Library.PresetIds.source600`, `detectorIntensity`, `polarizerLp` and `polarizerCpLeft`, and its doc's `pol-cp-right` (`:1008`) reads `PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. `paletteButtons`' CPL and CPR prebinds (`:2052-2053`) are `Some Library.PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft` and `Some Library.PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. (4) The four test files that named `SeedEntryIds` read `PresetIds`, and every other seeded preset id in them switches too, comments included. A fixture holds a preset or sample id as an `ElementValueId`, and a helper that wrapped a `string` id takes the `ElementValueId`, so no fixture re-wraps `.value` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin', which holds for fixtures). (a) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs`: the theory `AddElement lands PRE-BOUND to the kind's seeded default entry` (`:108-121`) cannot take a member through `InlineData`, so its rows carry the kind code only ("S", "D", "LP", "CP") and a private `expectedSeedOf (code : string) : ElementValueId` maps each code to its member; its name, its four rows and its assertions are unchanged. `AddElementBoundTo carries an explicit pre-bind — the CPR palette button's path` (`:135-140`), the palette fact (`:151-153`) and the detector binds (`:479-496`, `:587-593`) read the members. (b) `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs:532`: the expected prebinds are `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`, `Some PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft` and `Some PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. (c) `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`: `bind` (`:31-32`) takes `entryId : ElementValueId`; `glassFilm200Id`, `glassFilm600Id`, `glassPlate1mmId` and `euvMirrorId` (`:40-47`) hold the sample's `entryId` itself, and `BindValueId (ElementValueId glassFilm200Id)` (`:631`) passes `glassFilm200Id`. `withTunableSource` (`:36`) binds `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`, `:109` binds `PresetIds.heNe633` and `:280` binds `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`; `:308` and `:347` read the members, and the comments at `:307`, `:308` and `:318` name them. (d) `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`: `TableRun.sourceEntry` becomes an `ElementValueId`; `tableRun`'s `source` parameter follows, and `userSource` returns the `ElementValueId` it saves. `runOnTable` binds `run.sourceEntry` and `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` directly; `glassOnTable` and the two 600 nm runs pass `PresetIds.source600`; `xenon` is `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `euvAgainstWaveLength` passes `PresetIds.euvBeamline`. Its test-local user source "src-test-10nm" stays.

**Acceptance.** After the identities move, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke and ui-tests over the selected classes MUST pass with unchanged counts and every fact holding its assertion, the theory `AddElement lands PRE-BOUND to the kind's seeded default entry` keeping its four rows; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.
